{{Quote|Crow trusts no one and keeps to himself. The most anyone knows about him is that he's often found at the diner, hanging out with [[Bull]] and [[Bibi]].}}{{Portrait}}
Crow is a {{Rarity|Legendary}} [[Brawler]] that has low health, a normal reload speed, and a moderately low damaging attack that poisons enemies to deal extra damage over time with his long-ranged daggers. He was one of the 15 Brawlers who released at the first Beta launch. He has great mobility with his Super and his very fast movement speed. He attacks by firing 3 long-ranged daggers that inflict poison on his enemies and decrease healing. Crow's Super makes him jump, throwing poisonous daggers around him upon take-off and landing. His first Gadget, Instapoison, instantly deals remaining poison damage to all enemies, granting him a shield that absorbs damage and decays over time. His second Gadget, Slowing Toxin, throws a kunai that damages, slows, and poisons the enemy. His first Star Power, Extra Toxic, moderately decreases the damage output of a poisoned enemy. His second Star Power, Carrion Crow, makes enemies with less than half of their maximum health take much more damage from Crow's daggers. His Hypercharge, Utility Knives, makes his Super's daggers return to him upon take-off and landing.

==Attack: Switchblade==
{{Quote|Crow throws a triple threat of daggers. Enemies hit by the poisoned blades will take damage over time and have all healing effects reduced for the duration.}}Crow throws three long-ranged daggers simultaneously with a slight spread. These daggers damage enemies upon contact, while also inflicting poison to enemies over time. Poisoned enemies take a small amount of damage every second for up to 3 ticks. Poison effects do not stack with multiple daggers, but hitting an enemy that is already poisoned will refresh the poison effect's timer. Poisoned enemies have all healing sources reduced by 50%, but this doesn't affect [[Max]]'s Sneaky Sneakers Gadget. The healing reduction lasts for up to 4 seconds after the last hit from a dagger, as opposed to the poison's 3 seconds.

==Super: Swoop==
{{Quote|Crow takes to the skies, throwing a ring of poisoned daggers around him both on take-off and landing.}}Crow jumps into the air for 1 second and throws 14 daggers around him that spread out as they travel. He then lands, firing another set of 14 daggers around him upon landing, making him throw a total of 28 daggers with one Super. The daggers from his Super behave similarly to daggers from his main attack, but they have a shorter range of 7.33 tiles, and do not suppress healing. While in the air, Crow is completely immune to all damage besides status effects and damage applied over time.

==Gadgets==
===Instapoison===
{{Quote|Crow instantly deals remaining poison damage to all Crow-poisoned enemies and gains a shield for 150% of the value. Cooldown: 20 seconds.}}{{Gadget|1}}
Crow instantly deals remaining poison damage to all enemies, granting him a shield that is 150% of the total poison damage. The shield's health decays, and if an attack deals more damage than the shield's current health, the shield disappears and the Brawler with the shield is damaged by the remaining damage. Colette's attack and Super will deal damage based on the Brawler's max health when this shield is active. 

{{Quote|Refreshes poison duration.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, the poison duration is also refreshed.

===Slowing Toxin===
{{Quote|Throw a kunai that damages, slows, and poisons the first enemy hit for 2 sec. Cooldown: 17 seconds.}}{{Gadget|2}}
When aiming using the Gadget button, Crow throws a kunai that damages, poisons, and slows the enemy by 30% for 2 seconds. The poison damage is slightly higher than his regular poison and stacks on top of it, and also suppresses healing for 4 seconds.

{{Quote|The kunai also bounces to nearby targets, causing the same effect.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, the kunai bounces toward the next nearest enemy, similarly having the same effect. The bounce range is 6.67 tiles.

==Star Powers==
===Extra Toxic===
{{Quote|Crow's poison saps the strength of enemies, who deal 15% less damage while poisoned.}}{{StarPower|1}}
Crow's daggers apply an attack debuff, decreasing the damage output of a poisoned enemy by 15%. This Star Power only affects damage abilities. Affected enemies have an additional visual effect to indicate that this effect is active; there will be red swords falling down on the enemy. The effect is lost when the poison wears off. 

{{Quote|Crow deals 5% more damage for each enemy poisoned.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, Crow also deals 5% more damage to each enemy poisoned.

===Carrion Crow===
{{Quote|Crow deals +30% damage with his attack and Super to targets with 50% or less health.}}{{StarPower|2}}
If an enemy has 50% of their maximum health or less, Crow deals 30% extra damage per dagger with his main attack and Super to the enemy. The poison also deals 30% extra damage, so long as the enemy has the poison first applied when they are already below half their maximum health. In addition, their health bar turns pink instead of the usual red to indicate the Star Power's activation. The effect is lost if the enemy heals back above 50% health.

{{Quote|Crow's poison duration is increased by 1 sec.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, poisoned enemies take damage every second for up to 4 ticks, instead of regular 3.

==Hypercharge: Utility Knives==
{{Quote|Crow's knives are piercing and are returning like a boomerang.}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, daggers from Crow's Super now return to him after reaching their maximum range, and can also pierce through enemies. This effect applies to daggers fired when jumping and landing. However, the daggers can't travel through walls when being fired, but can return to Crow through walls. Crow also gains a 20% speed boost, as well as a 5% damage and shield boost.

{{Quote|Main attacks also pierce and return after reaching max distance, dealing 30% less damage when returning.}}{{Buffie|Hyper}}
With the Buffie, daggers from Crow's attack return to him after reaching their maximum range, dealing 30% less damage when returning, and piercing any enemies hit while the daggers are flying forward or traveling back to Crow like the daggers from his Hypercharged Super. Increased Hypercharge duration by 2 seconds.

==Mythic Gear: Enduring Toxins==
{{RemovedContent|section}}
{{Quote|Increases Crow's poison damage by 30%.}}{{Gear|Filename=CrowGear}}
With this Gear equipped, Crow's poison damage from his main attack and Super was increased by 30%, not taking into account any outside damage buffs or debuffs.

